d 'PLSSEM2': module to support partial least squares structural equation modeling (PLS-SEM) 
d
d      plssem2 fits partial least squares structural equation
d models (PLS-SEM), a variance-based, composite-based alternative
d to	covariance-based structural equation modeling (CB-SEM,
d e.g., sem and gsem).	The estimation follows the algorithm of
d Wold	  (1975) and Lohmöller (1989) as implemented in SmartPLS
d and in the Stata package plssem (Venturini and Mehmetoglu 2019),
d with	  the additions of blindfolding (Stone-Geisser Q2), HTMT
d discriminant validity (Henseler et al. 2015), bootstrap with	 
d bias-corrected and accelerated (BCa) confidence intervals (Efron
d 1987), higher-order constructs via the two-stage approach   
d (Becker et al. 2012; Sarstedt et al. 2019), and multi-group
d analysis based on the permutation test (Henseler et al. 2016). 
d
d KW: partial least squares
d KW: structural equation modeling
d
d Requires: Stata version 15.1
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260901
d
d Author: Wu LiangHai,  Anhui University of Technology
d Support: email agd2010@@yeah.net
d
d Author:   Wu Hanyan, Nanjing University of Aeronautics and Astronautics
d Support: email    2325476320@@qq.com
d
f plssem2_estat.ado
f plssem2_estat.sthlp
f plssem2_predict.ado
